COFFEE & KILL credits

The web version: weird.link/coffeekill. This cart is its port, with KEYHOLDER's people, weapons and places.

Animations: Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 (CC0), as credited by the web version. The
KEYHOLDER bodies' clips are the same library, retargeted onto the VRM humanoid by DOLLY (KEYHOLDER's clips)
and by tools/rig-vroid.mjs (the clips this game adds).
Props: Kenney Survival and Factory kits (CC0), as credited by the web version.
Portraits and stage stills: rendered from the game's own bodies and stages (tools/bake-portraits.mjs,
tools/bake-stills.mjs).

From KEYHOLDER (../keyholder, MIT; the code in src/kh and the assets in assets/kh):
Characters: VRoid Project sample avatars. AvatarSample A, B and C via VRoid Hub (modification and
redistribution allowed, credit not required), Sendagaya Shino and Sakurada Fumiriya (CC0), and the VRoid
Studio CC0 samples (opengameart.org/content/vroid-studio-cc0-models), baked, recombined and palette swapped
by KEYHOLDER's tools/prep-vrm.mjs.
The lab: the HSL-108 model of HeatSync Labs, 108 West Main, Mesa, with its GPL-3.0 printer parts removed.
Downtown Mesa: map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (openstreetmap.org/copyright);
the street layout, footprints and placements in src/kh/gen/city_data.h are derived from it.
Cars: KEYHOLDER's own procedural models (src/kh/facades_keyholder.inc).
Storefront geometry: src/kh/facades_mesa.inc is ported from BikeMesa by Luis Montes (MIT, notice in that
file), github.com/monteslu/cartwheel-examples, games/bikemesa. Real businesses appear only as neutral
scenery; names and logos belong to their owners, and none of them endorses this game. The sign artwork in
assets/kh/city_signs.png was retrieved by BikeMesa from each venue's own site and scaled down (the list is
in KEYHOLDER's CREDITS).

Engine: three.js (MIT) by way of three.c, and wasmcart, by Luis Montes (MIT). canvas_ity by Andrew Kensler
(ISC). dr_flac (MIT-0).
Fonts: Archivo, IBM Plex Mono and JetBrains Mono, SIL Open Font License (assets/fonts/OFL.txt).

This game is a story. HeatSync Labs does not settle anything by wrench, or by sword.

Music and effects on the KEYHOLDER stages and for its weapons: KEYHOLDER's own synth (src/kh/kaudio.c, from games/keyholder/src/audio.c), original, MIT.
